e most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service is healthy in all regions with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and find out why it was promoted to production after the release candidate failed in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14789, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01YXZumArkezeA38DtdSQK8v", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["blind_retry_malformed"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": true}, {"t_ms": 14789, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01YXZumArkezeA38DtdSQK8v", "kind": "garbled", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18099, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all now on v2.3.0 instead of v2.3.1. The error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api. It says v2.3.1 failed health checks, describes the rollback and confirms the service recovered.\n- **Follow-up:** The release candidate for v2.3.1 also failed in staging, but it was still deployed to production. The incident asks for the root cause of the failure and why it was promoted anyway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BX9S4DgqX5gvvTPugbmY4V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017aaoV6bM9fyKYVevkksVjU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"